# md5 of every input of banks/v6ms (md5sum format; `md5sum -c CODE.md5` from banks/v6ms/, or python banks/make_v6ms.py).
# The 9 closed rounds of 17: G1r01-G1r04 (SL), G2r01 (CB), G2r02 (SEL), G2r03 (INT), G3r01 (INV), G3r02 (CMQ).
#   writers/<lang>/<uid>.json  the 180 accepted writer files (all their templates; the verifier's verdicts are in clean/)
#   accept/<uid>.json          the 180 acceptance stamps; the project's differ in "path" only (an absolute path on the
#                              project's machine -> writers/<lang>/<uid>.json); the writer md5 inside each stamp is unchanged
#   clean/clean_<V>.json       the 37 verdict files (36 verifier units + the pilot unit, which re-judged G1r01 en/zh)
#   manifest/ vendor/          the unit plan (all 36 rounds; only the 9 above have templates) and v6ms.py's two vendored inputs
# v6ms.py differs from the project's copy (md5 b55f950d06f093acebf02efb6b5b4d9f): two comment / message strings no longer
# name a person, and accepted() / accepted_items() read a relative stamp path as relative to this folder (new helper
# _stamp). No edit touches the rows: SHIP_V6MS.md5 is the project's record and is reproduced byte for byte.
